> what do you think of:

@trask  I believe the following judgment logic is no longer necessary. Even if JMX is disabled, if a valid jmxName is configured, the value retrieved via BasicDataSource#getRegisteredJmxName will be the configured jmxName.
In older versions of commons-dbcp2, after specifying jmxName, jmxRegister would invoke MBeanServer.registerMBean, which in turn calls preRegister to assign registeredJmxName.
In newer versions, jmxRegister directly sets registeredJmxObjectName.

```
if (dataSourceName == null) {
  dataSourceName = dataSource.getJmxName();
  if (dataSourceName != null) {
    try {
      String name = new ObjectName(dataSourceName).getKeyProperty("name");
      if (name != null) {
        dataSourceName = name;
      }
    } catch (javax.management.MalformedObjectNameException ignored) {
      // Use the configured value as-is when it is not a valid ObjectName.
    }
  }
}
```

