@trask During the previous verification, we did use the legacy SDK for validation. After I tested with the new SDK, I can confirm it performs metric aggregation exactly as you described—it sums up metric values for entries with identical attributes.
However, this approach can easily obscure issues when an application has multiple connection pools. For instance, one connection pool may be under heavy load while another is barely utilized. Similarly, if two pools are configured with vastly different parameter limits: the one with a smaller threshold could already be overloaded, yet this problem would not be reflected in the aggregated metrics, leading to misleading observations during troubleshooting.
In my opinion, the drawbacks of this aggregation method outweigh the alternative solution of ensuring unique pool.name values by appending an auto-increment ID.

